rue] [17592186124332 1145 "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are $\\lambda_1={\\color{blue}4}$ and $\\lambda_2={\\color{red}3},$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to $\\lambda_1={\\color{blue}4},$ and\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to $\\lambda_2={\\color{red}3}.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535681 false] [17592186124520 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360873 13194139535681 true] [17592186124521 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360846 13194139535681 true] [17592186124521 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360880 13194139535681 true] [17592186124522 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360887 13194139535681 true] [17592186124522 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360894 13194139535681 true] [17592186124522 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360901 13194139535681 true] [17592186124523 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360839 13194139535681 true] [17592186124523 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360859 13194139535681 true] [17592186124523 1020 #edb/ref 17592186360866 13194139535681 true] [17592186125002 1017 #edb/ref 17592186123034 13194139535681 false] [17592186125002 1017 #edb/ref 17592186360853 13194139535681 true] [17592186125002 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535681 true] [17592186125002 1100 "Determine if the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}10 & -4 \\\\ 24 & -10\\end{aligned}]$ \nis diagonalizable or not, and if it is diagonalizable, find a corresponding diagonal matrix $D.$" 13194139535681 true] [17592186125002 1100 "If the matrix\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}10 & -4 \\\\ 24 & -10\\end{bmatrix}$\nis diagonalizable, find a corresponding diagonal matrix $D$." 13194139535681 false] [17592186125002 1145 "First, we find the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ by solving $det(A-\\lambda I)=0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}10-\\lambda  & -4 \\\\ 24 & -10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (10-\\lambda )(-10-\\lambda )-24\\cdot (-4) & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2.$ Since we get two distinct eigenvalues, the matrix $A$ is diagonalizable.\n\nNow, we construct the diagonal matrix $D,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535681 true] [17592186360839 1017 #edb/ref 17592186360840 13194139535681 true] [17592186360839 1089 "q-140039" 13194139535681 true] [17592186360839 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535681 true] [17592186360839 1100 "Consider the matrix $A$ for which ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1$ are eigenvalues, and\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nare the respective eigenvectors. What are the values of $a,b,c$ given that\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & b \\\\ c & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]{[\\begin{aligned}1 & b \\\\ c & -4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}?\n$$" 13194139535681 true] [17592186360839 1113 #uuid "e1fa7f70-96f7-5add-9ed6-bf21512ccb8d" 13194139535681 true] [17592186360839 1145 "Since the eigenvalues of the matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,$ we construct the diagonal matrix $D$ by writing the eigenvalues in the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, to construct the matrix $P,$ we simply write the respective eigenvectors as columns: \n\n- the $1$st column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2,$ and\n\n- the $2$nd column is the eigenvector corresponding to ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1.$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{align